-- R4 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md. This file was
-- not-ok/tc/every-rebinds-variable.l4: a NEGATIVE fixture, pinning the
-- `QuantifierVariableRebound` error, which refused `EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign t`
-- and told the author to write `Sign (EXACTLY t)` instead.
--
-- That error is retired, and the same text is now the positive case. Under R1
-- the quantifier's variable `t` is a lexical local, so the `t` in the action
-- REFERS to the member. It cannot be a fresh binder, because the name
-- resolves. The error's own message ("this would be a fresh name matching
-- anyone") became false the moment R1 landed, which is why the check went
-- rather than being reworded.
--
-- The traces are what the file is for: a STRANGER's signature must not
-- discharge the member's duty, and the member's own must.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING
    Stranger

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Countersign HAS signer IS AN Actor, `on behalf of` IS AN Actor

alice   MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob     MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
tenants MEANS LIST alice, bob

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each tenant signs` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

-- A STRANGER's signature does not discharge anyone's duty.
#TRACE `each tenant signs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Stranger DOES Sign Stranger AT 3

-- Each member signs. The barrier is satisfied and the HENCE fires.
#TRACE `each tenant signs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
    PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 4

-- The same narrowing in an argument slot the actor-agreement check does NOT
-- police. `Countersign t t` obliges each tenant to countersign ON HER OWN
-- behalf; before R1 the second `t` was a fresh binder matching ANY principal,
-- so Alice countersigning on Bob's behalf discharged her own duty. It no
-- longer does.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each tenant countersigns for herself` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Countersign t t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `each tenant countersigns for herself` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY alice DOES Countersign alice bob   AT 3
    PARTY bob   DOES Countersign bob   alice AT 4

#TRACE `each tenant countersigns for herself` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY alice DOES Countersign alice alice AT 3
    PARTY bob   DOES Countersign bob   bob   AT 4
